PD-mux capability/device consistency assert (multi-GPU M2, 2026-10-12).

Design: reports/multigpu_scaling_design_2026-10-12.md sec 2-5; audit R-4
(reports/audit/2026-10-12_multigpu_design/AUDIT_multigpu_design_rev1_2026-10-12.md).

WHAT IT GUARDS.  `initialize_stream_groups(gpu_id, config)` reads
`device = torch.cuda.current_device()` and uses it for exactly one thing:
`torch.cuda.get_device_capability(device)` handed to `divide_sm`, i.e. the
AUTO-GRID branch taken when the PD-mux config has no `manual_divisions`
(e.g. triage/pdmux_a100_smoke.yml).  Everything else in the
function -- SM total, green-context streams, plain streams -- is built from
`gpu_id` explicitly.  So a current_device/gpu_id mismatch can change a result
ONLY in the auto-grid branch, and only if the two GPUs differ in compute
capability; the assert sits inside that branch and nowhere else.
`manual_divisions` campaigns (55/59 of the *pdmux*.yml configs, scope audit
2026-09-22) never execute the line and are byte-for-byte unaffected.

WHY IT FIRES UNDER TP/DP > 1.  Scheduler.__init__ calls init_pdmux BEFORE the
TpModelWorker/ModelRunner is built, and ModelRunner is where
`torch.cuda.set_device(gpu_id)` happens (model_runner.py init_torch_distributed).
Nothing earlier in the spawned scheduler process sets the device, so at this
point current_device() is 0 for every rank (code-path reading; to be confirmed
on GPU in M2g).  With the stock launcher (gpu_id = base + dp*tp + tp_rank) every
scheduler with gpu_id != 0 therefore FAILS this assert in the auto-grid branch
-- deliberately: on a homogeneous node the capability read would happen to be
right, but by accident.  Two ways to run N>1 legitimately: a manual_divisions
config, or SGLANG_ONE_VISIBLE_DEVICE_PER_PROCESS=1 (maybe_reindex_device_id
then hands every process gpu_id 0 with a one-GPU CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, so
device == gpu_id == 0).

LINE-NEUTRAL: two same-line edits, so `pdmux_context.py:124-138` (cited in
results/hybrid_sched_s0/engine_porter_review_2026-09-30.md) does not move.
Applied by scripts/bootstrap/sync_engine_tree.sh (grep guard on
"PD-mux auto grid (divide_sm)") and hashed as manifest entry 26.

